# L §4.2, §8.4 (tally 2.1.7 B5, issue #98): the twin of L4_2_by_n_duration_load: a duration load can't see
# (n1 * 1 year) is refused at the key, RUN-DOMAIN, with the same words. Passes on 2.1.6's refcore too: it pins the
# phase boundary.
=== run.tally
model b5r
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "made up"

index y2 = year 2026..2040 by 2

input n1: int

def bad[q in y2]: date = start_of(q + n1 * 1 year)

ask a_bad: bad[2026]

version v
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  n1 = 1 "one"
=== expect
a_bad: refused: RUN-DOMAIN 2026 + 1 year: not a whole number of its periods (L §4.2)
  cut 2026-12-31
